(PRC-12 — `Mount "<source>" at "<target>" with type "<fstype>".` lowers to
 mount(2).
 Also covers: PRC-13 (the `with options "<options>"` clause is optional and
 accepted) and PRC-21 (Mount sets the error flag on failure).
 SAFETY: this probe is only safe because the process is unprivileged.
 mount(2) needs CAP_SYS_ADMIN, so every call here returns EPERM and no
 filesystem is touched. Run as root it would mount a real proc and a real
 tmpfs over the scratch directory. What is verified here is the ERROR
 path; the success path is not reachable without privilege.
 Ran, from the repo root:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-12.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the three-operand mount set the error flag
   the four-operand mount set the error flag
   execution continued past both
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_mount".
Mount "proc" at "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_mount" with type "proc".
On error print "the three-operand mount set the error flag".
Mount "tmpfs" at "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_mount" with type "tmpfs" with options "size=64m".
On error print "the four-operand mount set the error flag".
Remove the directory called "vf_scratch/process-control/scratch_mount".
print "execution continued past both".
